<title>MEXICO: Mexican crude port Dos Bocas closed.</title>
<headline>Mexican crude port Dos Bocas closed.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-05-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The key Mexican crude oil port of Dos Bocas was closed on Saturday as were other Gulf Coast ports of Veracruz, Tuxpan and Altamira, the Communications and Transport Ministry said.</p>
<p>It said the Gulf of Mexico coasts of Tamaulipas and Veracruz states were affected by strong northeasterly winds and four- to seven-foot waves. Further south, it said there was the likelihood of scattered heavy showers.</p>
<p>((-- Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9560))</p>
